# AMD GPU firmware, x86_64 only, on top of amd.list
# (rules/xxri-firmware-amd.make; the 32-bit system ships amd.list alone).
#
# Names are what amdgpu declares (MODULE_FIRMWARE, scripts/xxri-fw-requested.sh),
# minus what amd.list has, resolved against linux-firmware 20260810 by
# scripts/xxri-fw-select.py. If the driver wants a newer API than the release
# has, the newest one the release has is named instead.
#
# Scope: Polaris (RX 400/500), Vega, Navi 1x/2x/3x/4x (RX 5000-9000) and every
# Ryzen APU (Raven/Picasso, Renoir, Cezanne/Lucienne/Barcelo = green_sardine,
# Rembrandt = yellow_carp, Van Gogh, Phoenix/Hawk Point = gc_11_0_1/4, Strix).
# Left out: names the release doesn't have (SR-IOV *_cap.bin, ip_discovery.bin,
# one gc_11_0 toc/mes file), which are virtualisation and debug bits.
